Fixed the remaining per-serialized-object cache-backend round-trips in REST API list responses: the custom-field key lookup for nested representations, the Celery worker-count lookup in Job Queue `display` (which could also trigger an inline Celery broker inspection), and the tree-ancestry `display` lookup for tree models such as Location. Each is now additionally memoized in-process with a short TTL (bounded by the same staleness the underlying shared cache already tolerated), via a new `ProcessTTLCache` utility.
